---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import EmailCaptureForm from '../components/EmailCaptureForm.tsx';
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="GreenSquare · The brief that survives senior scrutiny"
  description="GreenSquare turns Claude or GPT into a disciplined decision advisor. It interrogates before it answers, then gives you an evidence-tagged recommendation you can defend."
  current="home"
>
  <!-- HERO — dark cinematic, abstract square field -->
  <section class="v-hero v-dark hero">
    <div class="v-hero__field" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="v-hero__nodes" aria-hidden="true">
      <i class="sq n1"></i><i class="sq n2"></i><i class="n3"></i><i class="sq n4"></i>
    </div>
    <div class="v-container v-hero__inner">
      <div class="v-split">
        <div class="v-reveal">
          <div class="v-eyebrow-row">
            <span class="v-notch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="v-label v-label--rule">It interrogates before it answers</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="v-display">The brief that survives senior scrutiny.</h1>
          <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">
            Think through any decision and come out with something you would stand behind. GreenSquare turns a
            generic AI into a disciplined thinking partner: it questions you before it answers, frames the real
            call, generates genuine options, and hands you an evidence-tagged recommendation, in markdown,
            identical on Claude and GPT.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="/product/">See how it works</a>
            <a class="v-link" href="/benchmark/">See the benchmark <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="v-reveal d1">
          <div class="v-terminal">
            <div class="v-terminal__bar"><span class="v-terminal__dot"></span> DECISION_BRIEF.md</div>
            <div class="v-terminal__body">
              <ul class="v-spec__list">
                <li><span class="n">/01</span> The decision, and why now</li>
                <li><span class="n">/02</span> The options, compared</li>
                <li><span class="n">/03</span> The recommendation</li>
                <li><span class="n">/04</span> Next steps</li>
                <li><span class="n">/05</span> What would change this call</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="spec-tags">
                <span class="v-tag">given</span><span class="v-tag">derived</span><span class="v-tag">unknown</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-terminal__foot">MARKDOWN OUTPUT <span class="v-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PULL-QUOTE — the one serif editorial beat -->
  <section class="v-section v-fill">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-reveal quote">
        <span class="v-notch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p class="v-serif">Most AI answers the question you typed. GreenSquare asks what a good adviser would ask first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THREE PILLARS — indexed capability list -->
  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-eyebrow-row"><span class="v-label">Three pillars</span></div>
      <h2 class="v-h2" style="max-width: 22ch;">Three things a generic answer skips.</h2>
      <div class="v-caplist">
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal">
          <span class="v-index">/01</span>
          <h3>It interrogates before it answers</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            It asks what a good adviser would ask first, tests the framing once, plays the situation back to
            you, and catches where your own answers contradict each other, before it produces anything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal d1">
          <span class="v-index">/02</span>
          <h3>It shows its evidence</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            Every claim the call rests on is tagged given, inferred or unknown, and the recommendation names
            the single assumption it stands on.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal d2">
          <span class="v-index">/03</span>
          <h3>It holds a consulting standard, on any model</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            The discipline is encoded in the file, so the output behaves the same on Claude or GPT, and scales
            effort to the stakes rather than over-engineering a small call.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EVIDENCE — terminal-green operational module -->
  <section class="v-section v-dark">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-reverse">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <div class="v-eyebrow-row"><span class="v-label v-label--rule">Evidence</span></div>
        <h2 class="v-h2">Same model, same question. Different brief.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-5);">
          Given only the question a real person would paste, a naked baseline reframes the problem, but sizes the
          risk at roughly 8% of revenue and never sees the mechanism that actually kills the deal. Loaded with
          the Decision, the same model interrogates the facts out, reaches close to 40% of the division, and
          lands a brief you could defend.
        </p>
        <a class="v-link" href="/benchmark/" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">Read the full comparison <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-terminal">
          <div class="v-terminal__bar"><span class="v-terminal__dot"></span> BENCHMARK · DEFENSIBLE_BRIEF</div>
          <div class="v-terminal__body">
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">NAKED BASELINE</span><span class="v-run__val">risk 8% &middot; structure 0/3</span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill is-muted" style="--w: 7%;"></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">INFORMED BASELINE</span><span class="v-run__val">structure 0/3</span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill is-muted" style="--w: 7%;"></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">THE DECISION</span><span class="v-run__val"><b>risk 40% &middot; structure 3/3</b></span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill" style="--w: 100%;"></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="v-terminal__foot">DESIGN-PHASE PILOT &middot; N=3 &middot; CASE A &middot; CLAUDE OPUS 4.8</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FREE FRAME -->
  <section class="v-section v-fill" id="frame">
    <div class="v-container v-split">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <div class="v-eyebrow-row"><span class="v-label">Start free</span></div>
        <h2 class="v-h2">Frame the decision before you evaluate anything.</h2>
        <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
          The Decision Frame is a free one-page tool that interrogates your decision before you weigh options:
          the real question, the false binary, the load-bearing assumption, and what you actually know. Then it
          hands you to the Decision to decide.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-card">
          <EmailCaptureForm client:visible buttonLabel="Send me the free Decision Frame" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPLIT CTA -->
  <section class="v-splitcta" aria-label="Get started">
    <div class="v-splitcta__panel v-splitcta__panel--graphite v-reveal">
      <span class="v-label" style="color: var(--v-signal);">Start free</span>
      <h2 class="v-h2" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem);">Start with the free frame.</h2>
      <a class="v-link" href="/decision-frame/">Free Decision Frame <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="v-splitcta__panel v-splitcta__panel--green v-reveal d1">
      <span class="v-label" style="color: var(--v-lime);">Ready when you are</span>
      <h2 class="v-h2">Make the call you would stand behind.</h2>
      <a class="v-link" href="/pricing/">Get the Decision, $49 <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(7rem, 13vh, 10.5rem); padding-bottom: clamp(4.5rem, 9vh, 7.5rem); }
  .hero .v-split { align-items: center; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--v-6); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-8); }
  .spec-tags { display: flex; gap: var(--v-2); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-2); }
  .quote { display: flex; gap: var(--v-6); align-items: flex-start; }
  .quote .v-notch { margin-top: 12px; flex: none; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero .v-terminal { margin-top: var(--v-6); }
  }
</style>
